!Editing Wiki Pages

Please note that this Wiki does not use quite the same markup language as the old one did. Please read [http://www.tikiwiki.org/tiki-index.php?page=WikiSyntax|Tiki Markup] for more information.

As a stylistic note, since __this__ Wiki is meant for content related to ((Lojban)), and ((Lojban)) makes very little use of capital letters, and in fact tends to look ugly if you capitalize it, we'd like to standardize on the use of double parentheses, ~np~(( ))~/np~, around links.

!Features

* E-mail-to-forum gatewaying!  You can now receive all changes to [http://lojban.org/tiki/tiki-view_forum.php?forumId=1|the WikiDiscuss forum] as e-mails, and replying to them will cause a forum post to occur!  Just [http://www.lojban.org/lsg2/|subscribe to the WikiDiscuss list].  If your mail program asks, you definately want to reply to the "Reply-To" address, not any others.
* User-selectable "modules".  Those are the things in the right and left sidebars with a big red X in their corners.  You can use the arrows to move them up and down, or the red X to remove them altogether if you don't like them.  You can configure them more carefully in the [http://lojban.org/tiki/tiki-user_assigned_modules.php|Modules page].
* User-selectable themes, some of which are very pretty.  Either use the "Style" dropdown box, which should be in the left sidebar at the bottom, or the [http://lojban.org/tiki/tiki-user_preferences.php|Preferences page].
* The shoutbox!  Just type something in it, and everyone who comes to the site will see what you have to say, for a while at least.

!Non-Features

There are a couple of things that I know people want that haven't been implemented yet. I may get around to them myself, or someone else on the dev team might.

You are mare than welcome to add stuff here.  If you do so, however, you should probably ((rlpowell|drop me an e-mail)).  You are also more than welcome to ((rlpowell|e-mail me)) if something on here has been sitting around for a while and you'd like to re-iterate your desire for it.

* Better comment handling.
** A "Last Changes" module for comments.
* Better e-mail notification features.
** E-mail notification on any wiki page change.
** E-mail notification on comments.